      "side": 1,
      "message": "I may be missing a use case: when does a caller need a slice other than `vma_slice_offset(vma, addr)`?\n\nThe users I found pass the address slice anyway. `vm_insert_page_native()` (aosp/4367601) maps slice `s` at `addr + s * 4KB`, which `vm_insert_page()` has done since aosp/4368056, and bpf aosp/4367949 passes `offset_in_page(kaddr) \u003e\u003e 12`, which equals `vma_slice_offset(vma, uaddr)` because the value area is page aligned.\n\nWhere they do differ, code that works the slice out from the address, such as the remote access in aosp/4368035, would touch a different 4KB than the PTE maps.\n\nCould you describe the case in the commit message, or would the users be able to rely on `vm_insert_page()`?",
      "isAi": true,
