      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:47:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be possible to leave `insert_page()` as it is? Right now the slice goes through `insert_page()` and all its callers, which mostly compute `vma_slice_offset()` just to pass it back.\n\nOne option is a single-slice insert in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h` next to `vma_insert_page_slices()`, for example `vma_insert_page_slice(vma, addr, page, prot, slice)` doing `get_locked_pte()`, `insert_page_into_pte_locked()` and `pte_unmap_unlock()`.\n\n`vm_insert_page_slice()` could then call `validate_page_before_insert()` and that helper, and `mm/memory.c` would barely change.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "406c948ead578d32dc8d3125cbb631acdaaf623a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
