      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:47:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this reverses what aosp/4368056 did for 4KB VMAs. There, each entry is a kernel page that gets all its slices, and `*num` counts kernel pages; with this change each entry fills one 4KB PTE.\n\nA caller passing kernel pages, as the kernel-doc describes, would get slice `(s + i) \u0026 3` of page `i` at the i-th 4KB PTE and the rest of the range unmapped. As far as I can see, that affects `vm_map_pages()` until aosp/4368010, the trace ring buffer until aosp/4367959, io_uring until aosp/4367948 rejects 4KB processes, and any vendor caller indefinitely.\n\nI don\u0027t think anything in this patch needs it. Would it be OK to keep aosp/4368056\u0027s meaning here, or to move this to its own patch together with the caller that needs it?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "406c948ead578d32dc8d3125cbb631acdaaf623a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
